## Interview 1 – Enthusiastic Student (Exploration & Participation)

**I:** Do you usually notice those big screens when you’re in the city?  
**P1:** Yeah, for sure. Especially that one in Queen Street. Last time I even saw some kid’s doodle up there, thought it was pretty cool.  

**I:** Oh nice, do you normally stop and have a look?  
**P1:** Yeah, I’ll stand there for a bit. Even if I don’t know the person, it’s just fun seeing people’s stuff get shown.  

**I:** And if you wanted to check out more of those artworks later on, how would you go about it?  
**P1:** Well, you can’t really, hey? Once it’s gone, it’s gone. Maybe take a photo, but that doesn’t feel the same. If there was an app where I could scroll through people’s stuff, like a little gallery, I’d definitely be on it heaps.  

**I:** Gotcha. Would you also wanna know exactly where those works had been shown?  
**P1:** Yeah, for sure. Like, if a map showed me “this piece was up at South Bank last week”, I’d probably head down there just to check it out. Feels a bit like a treasure hunt, you know?  

**I:** And say you saw on the map there’s a screen near you – would you wanna chuck something up yourself?  
**P1:** Haha, absolutely. But I’d want to pick the screen myself, not just have it go anywhere random. Feels more personal if I can choose.  

**I:** What about the drawing part – would you rather do it on-site or on your phone beforehand?  
**P1:** Phone, easy. I can do it on the train, at home, whenever. At the site it’s kinda rushed, maybe there’s a queue. On my phone I can muck around with colours, rub it out, start again, whenever the mood hits.  

**I:** So, ideal flow for you would be: flick through other people’s work, see the screens on a map, pick one, then draw on your phone and send it up?  
**P1:** Yeah, bang on. That’d be awesome, I’d be keen as to try it.  


## Interview 2 – Cautious Student (Control & Saving)

**I:** If you had the chance to put your own drawing on one of those big screens, would you give it a go?  
**P2:** Hmm… maybe. I’d be a bit nervous though. Like, if it looked dodgy and heaps of people saw it, that’d be a bit embarrassing.  

**I:** Fair call. What if the app let you preview how it’d look on the big screen first?  
**P2:** Oh yeah, that’d make a big difference. At least I’d know what I’m getting into. If it looked rubbish, I just wouldn’t post it. Feels safer that way.  

**I:** And if you were happy with it, would you want it to be quick and easy to get it up there?  
**P2:** Yeah, 100%. I wouldn’t want a whole bunch of steps. Just one button – send it and done.  

**I:** What about keeping your stuff – would you wanna save your drawings somewhere?  
**P2:** Definitely. Not everything needs to go on a screen, but I’d still wanna hang on to it. Having like a “My Page” with all my pieces would be awesome. Could show mates later, or just flick back through myself.  

**I:** So for you, the important bits are: being able to preview, quick posting, and saving everything in one spot, yeah?  
**P2:** Yeah, that’s pretty much it. Even if I don’t use the screen heaps, I’d use it to keep my stuff.  
